---
title: JSON schema reference
summary: Every object and field of the C4 workspace JSON format, generated from schema/c4.schema.json.
wide: true
---
{%- macro props(s) -%}
<section id="{{ s.anchor }}">
<h3>{{ s.title }}</h3>
{% if s.description %}<p>{{ s.description | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for p in s.properties %}
<tr id="{{ s.anchor }}-{{ p.name | lower | replace('$', '') }}"><td class="prop-name"><code>{{ p.name }}</code>{% if p.required %} <span class="req">required</span>{% endif %}</td><td>{{ p.type | safe }}</td><td>{{ p.description | safe }}</td></tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
</section>
{%- endmacro -%}

<p class="lead">Every object of the workspace format, generated from <a href="/c4.schema.json"><code>c4.schema.json</code></a> (JSON Schema 2020-12) when this site is built. All objects are closed: an unknown field is an error.</p>

<p>Point your editor to the schema for completion and validation: <code>"$schema": "path/to/schema/c4.schema.json"</code>. Rules the schema cannot express are listed in <a href="/validation/">Validation rules</a>.</p>

<nav class="note"><p><strong>On this page:</strong>
<a href="#workspace">Workspace</a> ·
{% for s in schema.objects %}<a href="#{{ s.anchor }}">{{ s.title }}</a> · {% endfor %}
<a href="#views">Views</a> ·
{% for s in schema.afterViews %}<a href="#{{ s.anchor }}">{{ s.title }}</a> · {% endfor %}
<a href="#common-types">Common types</a></p></nav>

<h2 id="structure">Structure</h2>

<pre><code>workspace
├── version, name, description, include[]
├── model
│   ├── people[]            <a href="#person">person</a>
│   ├── softwareSystems[]   <a href="#software-system">softwareSystem</a>
│   │   └── containers[]    <a href="#container">container</a>
│   │       └── components[] <a href="#component">component</a>
│   └── relationships[]     <a href="#relationship">relationship</a>
├── views[]                 <a href="#views">view</a> (by type)
└── styles
    ├── elements[]          <a href="#element-style">elementStyle</a>
    └── relationships[]     <a href="#relationship-style">relationshipStyle</a></code></pre>

<h2 id="model-objects">Workspace and model</h2>

{{ props(schema.workspace) }}
{% for s in schema.objects %}{{ props(s) }}{% endfor %}

<h2 id="views">Views</h2>

<p>A view is one of the five objects below, chosen by its <code>type</code>. See <a href="/views/">Views</a> for what each one shows.</p>

{% for s in schema.views %}{{ props(s) }}{% endfor %}

<h2 id="view-details">View details and styles</h2>

{% for s in schema.afterViews %}{{ props(s) }}{% endfor %}

<h2 id="common-types">Common types</h2>

{% for t in schema.common %}
<section id="{{ t.anchor }}">
<h3>{{ t.title }}</h3>
<p>{{ t.description | safe }}</p>
</section>
{% endfor %}

<section id="{{ schema.selector.anchor }}">
<h3>selector</h3>
<p>Used in <code>include</code> and <code>exclude</code>. One of:</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Selects</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for o in schema.selector.options %}
<tr><td>{{ o.form | safe }}</td><td>{{ o.meaning | safe }}</td></tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table></div>
</section>

{{ props(schema.property) }}
